from pathlib import Path
r=Path.cwd();p=r/'tools/build-guides.py';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig')
user=[
'Open the intended project or cache and choose Database schema in the upper-right page selector. Choose index in the kind selector and declared index in the state selector. Select a row. An index is a declared access structure that can affect reads, writes and storage. DPH shows what captured source declares; it does not connect to a database or measure whether the index helps.',
'The memo starts with Indexed table, Unique declared, Method, Storage kind and Ordered index members. Member order, explicit ASC or DESC and NULLS FIRST or LAST are retained. Not declared means absent from the captured declaration; it does not imply a default for an unknown database engine. Function or parenthesized expressions retain sanitized text. Their column dependencies remain unverified rather than being guessed from words in the expression.',
'Included columns are separate from key members. A predicate records the captured text of a partial or filtered index. Unique null treatment, explicit clustering, CONCURRENTLY, IF NOT EXISTS, ONLY, WITH storage options and TABLESPACE declarations remain separate facts. Text inside predicates and storage options is not evaluated or validated as database syntax. Literal values are omitted from the projection. Duplicate definitions remain separate, with the effective migration unresolved.',
'Scroll the command strip sideways to the relationship selector. Choose indexed table, indexed column, included column or SQL table reference and click Follow relationship. DPH opens the exact captured target and its required 250-row page. Missing or ambiguous tables and columns have no invented link. A SQL table reference means supported captured SQL names the same exact table; it does not establish that a query used this index or that its predicates or selected columns are covered. Zero references means no supported captured match, not that the index is unused. Navigation shows up to 250 references per index and 10000 across the projection, with total and shown counts.',
'Filter by index name, target table, method, predicate text, clustering, storage options or relationship status. First page and Next page show 250 matches. Unsupported member options, missing names or lists, malformed structures and unsupported tails remain explicit gaps. Open source uses attached-file generation and hash guards. Follow docs/guides/Database_Indexes_Run_and_Test.txt for launch, practice and developer validation steps. In the controlled fixture, IX_Composite links Data.Target, ordered a and b members, included note and a separate SQL resource.',
'For a performance investigation, ask the maintainer for an approved execution plan and measured workload observations. Record supplied runtime evidence through the existing Runtime observations workflow with contributor and run context. Source declarations and matching SQL references alone do not establish optimizer selection, physical size, timings, selectivity or an index recommendation.'
]
engineering=[
'TDPHDatabaseSchema.Inspect recognizes bounded CREATE INDEX declarations from already captured SQL resources. Supported headers retain explicit index names, optional UNIQUE, CLUSTERED or NONCLUSTERED, CONCURRENTLY, IF NOT EXISTS, ON ONLY and a qualified target table. Optional USING retains the declared method. The reference structure is PostgreSQL CREATE INDEX: https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/sql-createindex.html. Clustering keywords also retain captured structure from the supported cross-dialect subset; DPH does not validate combinations against a selected database dialect.',
'Ordered members retain position, column when it is a plain identifier, sanitized expression text, explicit sort and null order. Parenthesized and simple function expressions remain unresolved dependencies. INCLUDE accepts distinct plain column identifiers. Optional unique null treatment, balanced WITH option text, TABLESPACE and balanced WHERE predicate text are retained without evaluation. Empty lists or expressions, malformed name/list structure, unsupported member options or clause tails, excessive nesting and unsupported predicate subqueries remain gaps. Existing lexical, resource-size, token and row bounds apply; index expression nesting is limited to 128.',
'The existing relationship projection indexes exact table names and declaration-owned columns, using multiplicity counts. Index links target only unique captured table/column evidence. Duplicate table targets, columns and same-table index names remain explicit ambiguities or conflicts. Index records retain source SHA256, generation, statement line, resource byte extent, exact name and table scope. Effective migration order and live schema remain unknown. No schema migration, driver connection, SQL execution or runtime UI construction is introduced.',
'A separate exact-name lookup groups existing supported SQL table-reference rows. Index records show total and displayed reference counts and link to those captured evidence rows, capped at 250 references per index and 10000 across the projection. These links are labeled index use unobserved. They do not imply column coverage, plan selection or measured benefit. Absent supported matches cannot establish an unused index; quoted names and case are not normalized across dialects.',
'DPH.UI.Main.fmx adds index and declared index to the existing Object Inspector editable selectors. Main reuses the relationship selector, exact-ID Follow relationship navigation, 250-row paging, capture lifecycle and source guards. Search includes target table, method, predicate, storage kind and options. Details lead with index facts and explain evidence limitations before an investigation of performance can be justified.',
'Run tools/build-database-indexes.cmd elevated for actual project/resource capture, ordered composite and expression members, uniqueness and optional structure, literal omission, missing or ambiguous target evidence, malformed/unsupported grammar, persisted SQLite reopening, unchanged source/catalog/workspace, guarded source reading and native filtering/follow/replacement/normal/compact renders. The suite retains prior schema, column and key checks. Run key and schema regressions and tools/build-wp0.cmd for the application and serialized FMX bindings. Controlled practice stays in fixed ignored bin/database-indexes-validation.'
]
at=s.index('user_order = [');addition='USER.append(('+repr('Inspect indexes and performance evidence')+', '+repr(user)+'))\nENGINEERING.append(('+repr('Capture index structures and SQL reference evidence')+', '+repr(engineering)+'))\nfor chapters in (USER, ENGINEERING):\n for index, (heading, paragraphs) in enumerate(chapters):\n  chapters[index]=(heading,[p.replace("331 requirement records remain incomplete","330 requirement records remain incomplete") for p in paragraphs])\n\n';s=s[:at]+addition+s[at:]
at=s.index('user_order = [');s=s[:at]+s[at:].replace("'Inspect primary foreign and unique keys',", "'Inspect primary foreign and unique keys', 'Inspect indexes and performance evidence',",1)
s=s.replace("'guide_version': 20","'guide_version': 21");p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=r/'README.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig');s+='\nRequirement 05.06: Database schema now exposes captured indexes with ordered members/expressions, includes, predicates, methods and storage declarations. Exact captured table, column and SQL reference links reuse Follow relationship. SQL references do not prove index use or performance benefit. See docs/guides/Database_Indexes_Run_and_Test.txt.\n';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
